# Binary, or byte-exact on purpose: no end-of-line translation in either direction. The .pnml
# fixtures are CRLF as committed and several tests compare them byte for byte.
*.ico -text
*.png -text
*.PNG -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.gif -text
*.pnml -text

# Git LFS is reserved for assets big enough to be worth the indirection - in practice just the
# demo recordings under docs/, which are ~500 KB each. Everything else stays a plain Git blob.
# Listed last so this filter wins over the bare patterns above.
#
# The app's own assets were in LFS until 2.2.2, and that release shipped broken because of it:
# `actions/checkout` does not fetch LFS unless asked, so the release build packaged 128-byte
# pointer stubs named hand_icon.png, pl.png, trans.png and friends. They loaded as resources,
# decoded as nothing, and the toolbar came up with blank buttons. An icon that costs 400 bytes
# to store outright should never depend on a second fetch protocol going right.
docs/media/*.gif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

*.sh text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
